WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.760
Netflix might be the top dog when it comes
to online video subscription services, but

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.510
Amazon Prime Video is mounting a real challenge
to that title.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:13.420
In fact, Amazon Prime actually has more subscribers,
though many of them haven't even checked out

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.509
the company's video service.

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:19.199
If you're one of those people, or you're just
wondering what exactly they have to offer,

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:23.650
here's a look at some of the hidden gems available
on Amazon Prime Instant Video.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.240
Paradise Lost: The Child Murders at Robin
Hood Hills

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.220
If you love true crime dramas, then don't
miss your chance to watch this gripping and

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.700
moving documentary about one of the most notorious
multiple killings in recent history.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.130
Paradise Lost chronicles the tale of the "West
Memphis Three" — three teenagers tried and

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.780
convicted for the murders of three boys in
West Memphis, Arkansas.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:48.670
"I think the cops just can't find who done
it, and they gotta put it on somebody."

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.540
It's a chilling look at both the brutal murders,
and the witch hunt that led to convictions

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.740
against the three suspects, who were finally
released from prison nearly two decades later.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.900
"So like I'm the West Memphis Boogie Man.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.759
Little kids will be looking under their bed
before they go to bed. They be puttin me under there."

00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:05.840
Monster

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.210
Roger Ebert called Charlize Theron's portrayal
of serial killer Aileen Wuornos in Monster

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.810
"one of the greatest performances in the history
of the cinema."

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.710
Theron ended up winning 17 awards for the
role, including the Academy Award and Golden

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.880
Globe for Best Actress, with many critics
and audience members failing to even recognize

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.859
Theron thanks to a truly transformative performance.

00:01:23.859 --> 00:01:30.070
"So I'm real good with people and um, um I
know how to work a rolodex."

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.979
The harrowing true crime story isn't for everyone,
but if you love quality cinema, it might be

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:36.189
for you.

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:37.189
Adventureland

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:41.799
Jesse Eisenberg, Kristen Stewart, Kristen
Wiig, and Bill Hader headline Adventureland,

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:44.329
an irreverent comedy set at a rundown amusement
park.

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:46.449
"You don't know what I'm capable of!

00:01:46.449 --> 00:01:46.949
Come on!

00:01:46.949 --> 00:01:47.440
Please!"

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.679
At times touching and sweet, at others uproariously
funny, Adventureland is a great summer coming-of-age

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:57.350
flick that mixes nostalgia with offbeat humor
to create an unexpectedly moving movie experience.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.200
"What the hell was that?"

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.689
"It's just my life."

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:01.689
Selma

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:07.079
In this critically acclaimed historical drama,
Selma takes us on a journey to 1965, as Dr.

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:12.100
Martin Luther King and other voting rights
activists lead protesters on a 54-mile-long

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.360
march from Selma to Montgomery, Alabama.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.100
By highlighting racial injustice with these
marches — some of which were televised as

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.960
troopers beat and attacked the protesters
— the disenfranchisement of black voters

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.420
finally came to an end after the passage of
the Voting Rights Act later that year.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.250
Selma doesn't pull any punches, and dramatically
depicts the brutalization and killing of activists

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.560
and innocents in a seminal moment of American
history that resonates as strongly now as

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.020
ever.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.320
Under the Skin

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.260
Scarlett Johansson delivers a spellbinding
performance in Under the Skin as a mysterious

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.180
alien who preys on men in Scotland.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.580
The movie takes on the alien's perspective
of our world, and she exhibits callous disinterest

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.880
in the things that make the human experience
unique — the urge to comfort a crying baby,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.440
savoring the flavor of food, or the simple
enjoyment of music.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.530
And that's the heart of this film's magnetic
draw — by showing the audience our world

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.830
from an alien perspective, it makes the point
clear that the meaning of everything really

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.420
is in the eye of the beholder.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.160
Bone Tomahawk

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.160
We like Kurt Russell.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.790
We love horror films.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.730
We really love Tombstone.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:19.270
So when a director makes a genre-bending western
horror film starring Kurt Russell as a hard-nosed

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.491
lawman who has to defeat a clan of cannibals,
it's pretty much guaranteed that we're going

00:03:23.491 --> 00:03:24.491
to lose our minds over it.

00:03:24.491 --> 00:03:28.730
Bone Tomahawk is just as awesome as it sounds,
with Russell starring as Sheriff Franklin

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.960
Hunt, who must figure out how to defeat the
cannibals holed up in the "Valley of Starving

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.320
Men" before they can murder more of the citizens
of the small town he's sworn to defend.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.760
Heck yeah!

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.760
Ex Machina

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.670
If you love science fiction films about robots
or artificial intelligence, but hate their

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:48.440
constantly rehashed plots, Ex Machina is the
remedy you've been searching for.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:52.620
This independent movie takes common science
fiction tropes and turns them upside down,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.820
as a computer programmer Caleb accepts an
invitation to administer the Turing intelligence

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.340
test to a humanoid robot named Ava.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.371
What follows is an intricate plot with elements
of sci-fi, horror, psychological drama, and

00:04:03.371 --> 00:04:07.360
thrills to keep you entertained and engaged
through numerous unexpected twists.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:12.020
With exceptional writing and a stellar performance
by Alicia Vikander as Ava, Ex Machina will

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.840
keep you at the edge of your seat.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.090
And best of all?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.250
It has dancing!

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.650
"Tryin to find a friend."

00:04:18.739 --> 00:04:20.519
This movie's got everything!

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:21.519
Thanks for watching!

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:23.610
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.690
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

